  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "A service mesh is a dedicated infrastructure layer for managing service-to-service communication within a microservices architecture, providing traffic management, mutual TLS encryption, observability, and policy enforcement transparently to application code through sidecar proxies or eBPF-based data planes. It decouples operational concerns\u2014load balancing, retries, circuit breaking, telemetry\u2014from business logic, enabling consistent reliability and security across heterogeneous services.",
